1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,620
you

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,260
Krishnamurti in dialogue with Dr. Alan W. Anderson.

3
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:44,470
J. Krishnamurti was born in

4
00:00:44,470 --> 00:00:46,300
South India and educated in England.

5
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:48,870
For the past 40 years, he

6
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:50,680
has been speaking in the United States,

7
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:54,300
Europe, India, Australia, and other parts of the world.

8
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:56,900
From the outset of his life's work,

9
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:58,920
he repudiated all connections

10
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:00,940
with organized religions and ideologies

11
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:03,920
and said that his only concern

12
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:06,900
was to set men absolutely unconditionally free.

13
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:10,440
He is the author of many books, among them

14
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:14,060
The Awakening of Intelligence, The Urgency of Change,

15
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,920
Freedom from the Known, and The Flight of the Eagle.

16
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:21,550
This is one of a series of

17
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:24,120
dialogues between Krishnamurti and Dr. Alan W. Anderson,

18
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,880
who is professor of religious studies at San Diego,

19
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:29,610
San Diego State University, where he teaches

20
00:01:29,610 --> 00:01:32,320
Indian and Chinese scriptures and the oracular tradition.

21
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:36,740
Dr. Anderson, a published poet, received his degree

22
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:40,300
from Columbia University and the Union Theological Seminary.

23
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:43,320
He has been honored with a Distinguished

24
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:45,940
Teaching Award from the California State Universities.

25
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:50,770
Mr. Krishnamurti, in our

26
00:01:50,770 --> 00:01:53,200
previous conversation, I was extremely

27
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:56,840
delighted, for myself at least,

28
00:01:57,460 --> 00:02:00,700
that we had made the distinction in

29
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,940
terms of the relation between knowledge and

30
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,680
self-transformation between,

31
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:09,720
on the one hand,

32
00:02:10,539 --> 00:02:13,360
the relationship that I sustained to the world, as

33
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:16,180
the world is me and I am the world,

34
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:21,140
and on the other hand, this dysfunctional condition,

35
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:24,440
which indicates in your phrase

36
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:26,880
that a person's

37
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,210
a person is involved in thinking

38
00:02:30,210 --> 00:02:33,220
that the description is the described.

39
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:38,980
It would appear then that something must be done

40
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:43,660
to bring about a change in the individual,

41
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:47,260
and going back to our use of the word individual,

42
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,250
we could say, and you used the word

43
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:53,200
earlier, that we are dealing with an observer.

44
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,420
So if the individual is not

45
00:02:56,420 --> 00:02:58,420
to make the mistake

46
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:02,760
of taking the description for the described,

47
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:05,820
then he must, as an observer,

48
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:09,820
relate to the observed in a

49
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:12,660
particular way that is totally different

50
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:16,239
from the way he has been in his confusion.

51
00:03:16,339 --> 00:03:18,609
I thought perhaps in this

52
00:03:18,609 --> 00:03:20,880
particular conversation, if we pursued that,

53
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:23,270
it would be a link directly

54
00:03:23,270 --> 00:03:25,560
with what we had said prior.

55
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:29,560
What we said previously, wasn't it, that

56
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:35,060
there must be a quality of freedom

57
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:38,560
from the known,

58
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:45,060
otherwise the known is merely the repetitive of the past,

59
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:47,800
the tradition, the image and so on.

60
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:55,500
The past, surely, sir, is the observer.

61
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:56,560
Yes.

62
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:02,560
The past is the accumulated knowledge,

63
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:08,060
as the me and the we, they and us,

64
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:19,060
the observer is put together by thought as the past.

65
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:21,060
Thought is the past.

66
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:25,560
Thought is never free.

67
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,560
Thought is never new,

68
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:32,560
because thought is the response of the past

69
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:36,060
as knowledge, as experience, as memory.

70
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:40,060
Yes, I follow that.

71
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:43,560
And the observer, when he observes,

72
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:50,560
is observing with the memories, experiences, knowledge,

73
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:55,060
hurts, despairs, hopes, all that, with all that,

74
00:04:55,560 --> 00:05:01,060
and that is the background he looks at the observed.

75
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:07,560
So, the observer then becomes separate from the observed.

76
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:14,060
Is the observer different from the observed,

77
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:16,060
which we'll go into presently later on?

78
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,060
Yes, right.

79
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:19,560
That leads to all kinds of other things.

80
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:22,060
So,

81
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:27,060
when we are talking of freedom from the known,

82
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:32,060
we are talking about the freedom from the observer.

83
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:35,560
The observer, yes.

84
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,560
And the observer is

85
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:43,060
the tradition, the past,

86
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:49,560
the conditioned mind that looks at things,

87
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:53,560
looks at itself, looks at the world,

88
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,560
looks at me and so on.

89
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,560
So, the observer is always dividing.

90
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,560
The observer is the past,

91
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:06,560
and therefore he cannot observe wholly.

92
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:15,560
If a person uses the first person pronoun,

93
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,560
I,

94
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:22,560
while he is taking the description for the described,

95
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,060
this is the observer he

96
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,560
refers to when he says, I.

97
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,560
Yes.

98
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:27,560
Yes, please do go on.

99
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,560
I is the past.

100
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,560
I see.

101
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:36,560
I is the whole structure of what has been.

102
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:40,560
The remembrances, the memories, the hurts,

103
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:42,560
the various demands,

104
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:46,560
all that is put together,

105
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,560
is the past.

106
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,560
In the world, the I,

107
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,560
who is the observer.

108
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:56,560
And therefore, division.

109
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,560
The observer and the observed.

110
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:03,560
The observer who thinks he is a Christian

111
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:07,560
and observes a non-Christian or a communist,

112
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:08,560
is this division,

113
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:12,560
this attitude of mind which

114
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,560
observes

115
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:20,560
with a conditioned responses,

116
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:24,560
with memories and so on.

117
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:26,560
So, that is the known.

118
00:07:29,666 --> 00:07:30,166
下一次

119
00:07:30,754 --> 00:07:33,934
I mean, I think that is logically so.

120
00:07:33,934 --> 00:07:36,514
Oh no, it follows precisely from what you've said.

121
00:07:36,514 --> 00:07:41,254
Yes. So, we are asking, can the mind,

122
00:07:41,274 --> 00:07:43,254
or the whole structure,

123
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:48,994
can the mind be free from the known?

124
00:07:49,674 --> 00:07:55,854
Otherwise the repetitious action,

125
00:07:55,854 --> 00:08:01,474
repetitious attitudes, repetitious ideologies will go on,

126
00:08:01,494 --> 00:08:06,734
modified, changed, but in the same direction.

127
00:08:06,734 --> 00:08:08,214
So...

128
00:08:08,234 --> 00:08:10,134
Oh, go ahead. I was just going to say something,

129
00:08:10,134 --> 00:08:11,394
but I think I'll let it

130
00:08:11,394 --> 00:08:12,654
wait until you finish what you've said.

131
00:08:12,654 --> 00:08:18,734
Yes. So, what is this freedom from the known?

132
00:08:18,754 --> 00:08:21,854
I think that's very important to understand,

133
00:08:21,854 --> 00:08:25,854
because any creative action

134
00:08:25,874 --> 00:08:29,734
– I'm using the word creative in its original sense,

135
00:08:29,734 --> 00:08:33,874
not in the sense creative writing, creative...

136
00:08:33,874 --> 00:08:34,933
I know what you're...

137
00:08:34,953 --> 00:08:39,034
...bakery, creative essay, creative pictures,

138
00:08:39,034 --> 00:08:40,634
I'm not talking in those sense.

139
00:08:40,654 --> 00:08:43,433
In the deeper sense of that word,

140
00:08:43,453 --> 00:08:51,614
creative means something totally new being born.

141
00:08:52,094 --> 00:08:55,854
I mean, it's not creative, it's merely repetitive, modified.

142
00:08:55,873 --> 00:08:58,313
Changed, what the past.

143
00:08:58,313 --> 00:09:03,034
So, unless there is a freedom from the known,

144
00:09:03,034 --> 00:09:07,854
there is no creative action at all.

145
00:09:09,793 --> 00:09:19,754
Which is, freedom implies not the negation of the known,

146
00:09:19,774 --> 00:09:22,574
but the understanding of the known,

147
00:09:22,594 --> 00:09:25,854
and that understanding brings about

148
00:09:25,873 --> 00:09:29,994
an intelligence which is the very essence of freedom.

149
00:09:30,013 --> 00:09:33,614
Right. I'd like to make sure

150
00:09:33,634 --> 00:09:36,974
that I've understood your use of this word, creative.

151
00:09:36,994 --> 00:09:37,774
Yes, that's why I...

152
00:09:37,793 --> 00:09:39,814
It seems to me very, very important.

153
00:09:39,814 --> 00:09:42,374
Yes.

154
00:09:42,394 --> 00:09:44,474
People who use the word creative

155
00:09:44,494 --> 00:09:46,374
in the sense that you described,

156
00:09:46,394 --> 00:09:47,613
creative this, that and the other...

157
00:09:47,613 --> 00:09:48,694
That's a horror.

158
00:09:48,694 --> 00:09:51,273
That is the dreadful way of using that word.

159
00:09:51,273 --> 00:09:55,794
Because what the issue is of their activity,

160
00:09:55,794 --> 00:09:58,174
is something merely novel.

161
00:09:58,194 --> 00:09:59,894
Novel, novel. That's right.

162
00:09:59,914 --> 00:10:03,574
Not radically new, but novel.

163
00:10:03,594 --> 00:10:07,034
It's like creative writing, teaching creative writing.

164
00:10:07,053 --> 00:10:08,734
It's so absurd.

165
00:10:08,754 --> 00:10:10,294
Exactly. Yes.

166
00:10:10,314 --> 00:10:13,934
Now I do, I think, grasp precisely

167
00:10:13,954 --> 00:10:15,854
the distinction that you've made.

168
00:10:15,874 --> 00:10:20,394
And I must say I fully agree with that.

169
00:10:20,414 --> 00:10:25,713
Unless you feel new, you can't create anything new.

170
00:10:25,794 --> 00:10:26,794
That's right.

171
00:10:26,814 --> 00:10:33,074
And the person who imagines that he is creative

172
00:10:33,094 --> 00:10:37,074
in this other sense that we pointed to,

173
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:41,794
is a person whose reference for his activity

174
00:10:41,814 --> 00:10:44,794
is this observer that we mentioned,

175
00:10:44,814 --> 00:10:46,674
that is tied to the past.

176
00:10:46,694 --> 00:10:47,674
Yes, that's right.

177
00:10:47,694 --> 00:10:52,074
So even if something does appear that is really

178
00:10:52,094 --> 00:10:54,773
extraordinarily novel, merely,

179
00:10:54,794 --> 00:10:55,234
Yes.

180
00:10:55,234 --> 00:10:57,734
but still extraordinarily novel,

181
00:10:57,754 --> 00:10:59,234
they are kidding themselves.

182
00:10:59,254 --> 00:11:00,734
The novel is not the creative.

183
00:11:00,754 --> 00:11:01,474
Exactly.

184
00:11:01,493 --> 00:11:03,234
The novel is just the novel.

185
00:11:03,254 --> 00:11:05,244
Right. And today especially, it

186
00:11:05,244 --> 00:11:07,234
seems to me, in our culture,

187
00:11:07,254 --> 00:11:09,234
we've become hysterical about this,

188
00:11:09,254 --> 00:11:11,234
because in order to be creative,

189
00:11:11,254 --> 00:11:14,234
one simply must rack his brains

190
00:11:14,254 --> 00:11:17,234
in order to produce something which in itself

191
00:11:17,254 --> 00:11:20,234
is bizarre enough to get attention.

192
00:11:20,254 --> 00:11:24,234
That's right. Attention, success.

193
00:11:24,254 --> 00:11:25,234
Yes.

194
00:11:25,254 --> 00:11:28,734
It has to be novel to the degree

195
00:11:28,754 --> 00:11:31,734
that I feel knocked on the head by it.

196
00:11:31,754 --> 00:11:33,234
Yes, eccentric and all the rest of it.

197
00:11:33,254 --> 00:11:37,234
Exactly. But if that tension is increased,

198
00:11:37,254 --> 00:11:39,234
then with each succeeding generation,

199
00:11:39,254 --> 00:11:42,734
the person is put to tremendous stress,

200
00:11:42,754 --> 00:11:45,734
not to repeat the past, which he can't help repeating.

201
00:11:45,754 --> 00:11:47,734
Repeating, quite. That's why I say,

202
00:11:47,754 --> 00:11:48,734
Exactly.

203
00:11:48,754 --> 00:11:54,234
freedom is one thing and knowledge is another.

204
00:11:54,254 --> 00:11:58,734
We must relate the two and see whether the mind

205
00:11:58,754 --> 00:12:02,734
can be free from knowledge.

206
00:12:02,754 --> 00:12:04,994
We won't go into it now.

207
00:12:04,994 --> 00:12:07,234
This is real meditation for me.

208
00:12:07,254 --> 00:12:09,234
You follow, sir? Yes, I do.

209
00:12:09,254 --> 00:12:13,234
Because when we talk about meditation,

210
00:12:13,254 --> 00:12:17,234
we'll go into it, but...

211
00:12:17,254 --> 00:12:23,234
You see, whether the brain can record

212
00:12:23,234 --> 00:12:28,234
and be free not to record.

213
00:12:28,254 --> 00:12:34,234
The brain to record and operate when necessary

214
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:37,234
in the recording, in memory, in knowledge,

215
00:12:37,254 --> 00:12:42,234
and be free to observe without the observer.

216
00:12:42,254 --> 00:12:43,234
You see?

217
00:12:43,254 --> 00:12:45,234
Oh, yes, yes, I see.

218
00:12:45,254 --> 00:12:50,234
That distinction seems to me absolutely necessary.

219
00:12:50,254 --> 00:12:52,234
Otherwise it wouldn't be intelligible.

220
00:12:52,254 --> 00:12:53,194
No.

221
00:12:53,194 --> 00:12:54,194
No, yes.

222
00:12:54,214 --> 00:13:02,194
So, knowledge means, is necessary to act,

223
00:13:02,214 --> 00:13:05,204
in the sense, my going home

224
00:13:05,204 --> 00:13:08,194
from here to the place I live.

225
00:13:08,214 --> 00:13:10,194
I must have knowledge.

226
00:13:10,214 --> 00:13:14,194
I must have knowledge to speak English.

227
00:13:14,214 --> 00:13:15,704
I must have knowledge to

228
00:13:15,704 --> 00:13:17,194
write a letter and so on.

229
00:13:17,214 --> 00:13:19,194
Everything.

230
00:13:19,214 --> 00:13:22,194
The knowledge as function

231
00:13:22,194 --> 00:13:26,194
is mechanical function is necessary.

232
00:13:26,214 --> 00:13:29,204
Now, if I use that

233
00:13:29,204 --> 00:13:32,194
knowledge in my relationship with you,

234
00:13:32,214 --> 00:13:34,194
another human being,

235
00:13:34,214 --> 00:13:37,194
I am bringing about a barrier,

236
00:13:37,214 --> 00:13:40,194
a division between you and me,

237
00:13:40,214 --> 00:13:43,194
who is the observer.

238
00:13:43,214 --> 00:13:46,194
If I am making myself clear.

239
00:13:46,214 --> 00:13:48,194
And I am the observed in that case.

240
00:13:48,214 --> 00:13:49,194
Yes.

241
00:13:49,214 --> 00:13:50,194
Right, in that context.

242
00:13:50,194 --> 00:13:54,194
That is, knowledge in relationship,

243
00:13:54,214 --> 00:13:59,194
in human relationship, is destructive.

244
00:13:59,214 --> 00:14:02,194
That is, knowledge,

245
00:14:02,214 --> 00:14:07,194
which is the tradition, the memory, the image,

246
00:14:07,214 --> 00:14:13,194
which the mind has built about you,

247
00:14:13,214 --> 00:14:16,194
when we are related together,

248
00:14:16,214 --> 00:14:19,194
that knowledge is separating.

249
00:14:19,194 --> 00:14:26,194
And therefore creates conflict in that relationship.

250
00:14:26,214 --> 00:14:29,194
As we said earlier, where there is division,

251
00:14:29,214 --> 00:14:32,194
there must be conflict.

252
00:14:32,214 --> 00:14:34,194
Division between India and Pakistan,

253
00:14:34,214 --> 00:14:37,194
India and America, Russia and all that,

254
00:14:37,214 --> 00:14:41,194
this divisive activity,

255
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:44,194
politically, religiously, economically, socially,

256
00:14:44,214 --> 00:14:48,194
in every way, must inevitably bring conflict,

257
00:14:48,194 --> 00:14:52,194
and therefore violence.

258
00:14:52,214 --> 00:14:54,194
That is obvious.

259
00:14:54,214 --> 00:14:56,194
Exactly.

260
00:14:56,214 --> 00:15:00,194
Now, when in relationship,

261
00:15:00,214 --> 00:15:02,194
in human relationship,

262
00:15:02,214 --> 00:15:06,194
knowledge comes between,

263
00:15:06,214 --> 00:15:11,194
then in that relationship there must be conflict.

264
00:15:11,214 --> 00:15:14,194
Between a wife, husband and wife, boy and girl,

265
00:15:14,214 --> 00:15:17,194
wherever there is the operation of,

266
00:15:17,194 --> 00:15:21,194
the observer who is the past, who is knowledge,

267
00:15:21,214 --> 00:15:25,194
in that activity there is division,

268
00:15:25,214 --> 00:15:29,194
and therefore conflict in relationship.

269
00:15:29,214 --> 00:15:33,194
So now the question that comes up next

270
00:15:33,214 --> 00:15:39,194
is the one of freedom from being subject

271
00:15:39,214 --> 00:15:42,194
to this repetitive round.

272
00:15:42,214 --> 00:15:43,194
That's right.

273
00:15:43,214 --> 00:15:44,194
Good.

274
00:15:44,214 --> 00:15:47,194
Now, is that possible? You follow, sir?

275
00:15:47,214 --> 00:15:51,194
It's an immense question because

276
00:15:51,214 --> 00:15:57,194
human beings live in relationship.

277
00:15:57,214 --> 00:15:58,194
Yes.

278
00:15:58,214 --> 00:16:03,194
There is no life without relationship.

279
00:16:03,214 --> 00:16:08,194
Life means to be related.

280
00:16:08,214 --> 00:16:10,194
Exactly.

281
00:16:10,214 --> 00:16:12,194
People who retire into a monastery and all that,

282
00:16:12,214 --> 00:16:14,194
they are still related,

283
00:16:14,214 --> 00:16:17,194
however much they might like to think they are alone,

284
00:16:17,214 --> 00:16:19,194
they are actually related.

285
00:16:19,214 --> 00:16:20,194
Yes.

286
00:16:20,214 --> 00:16:22,194
Related to the past.

287
00:16:22,214 --> 00:16:24,194
Oh yes, very much so.

288
00:16:24,214 --> 00:16:26,194
To their saviour, to their Christ,

289
00:16:26,214 --> 00:16:28,194
to their Buddha, to their...

290
00:16:28,214 --> 00:16:30,194
You follow? All that, they are related to the past.

291
00:16:30,214 --> 00:16:31,194
And their rule.

292
00:16:31,214 --> 00:16:33,194
And their rule is everywhere.

293
00:16:33,214 --> 00:16:35,194
They live in the past.

294
00:16:35,214 --> 00:16:41,194
And therefore they are the most destructive people,

295
00:16:41,214 --> 00:16:43,714
because they are not creative in

296
00:16:43,714 --> 00:16:46,214
the deeper sense of that word.

297
00:16:46,234 --> 00:16:49,214
No, and they also,

298
00:16:49,234 --> 00:16:52,214
insofar as they are involved in this confusion

299
00:16:52,234 --> 00:16:56,214
that you have been talking about,

300
00:16:56,234 --> 00:16:59,214
are not even producing anything novel.

301
00:16:59,234 --> 00:17:01,214
Not that that means anything,

302
00:17:01,234 --> 00:17:04,214
but perhaps that would rather radically...

303
00:17:04,233 --> 00:17:08,214
The novel would be for a man who is talkative

304
00:17:08,233 --> 00:17:10,214
to enter a monastery where they don't talk.

305
00:17:10,233 --> 00:17:12,223
That's a novel to him,

306
00:17:12,223 --> 00:17:14,214
and he said that's a miracle.

307
00:17:14,214 --> 00:17:16,214
Right.

308
00:17:16,233 --> 00:17:19,214
So, our problem then is,

309
00:17:19,233 --> 00:17:26,214
what place has knowledge in human relationship?

310
00:17:26,233 --> 00:17:28,214
Yes, that's the problem.

311
00:17:28,233 --> 00:17:30,214
That's one problem.

312
00:17:30,234 --> 00:17:31,214
Yes.

313
00:17:31,234 --> 00:17:35,214
Because relationship with human beings

314
00:17:35,234 --> 00:17:38,214
is the highest importance, obviously.

315
00:17:38,234 --> 00:17:40,214
Because out of that relationship

316
00:17:40,234 --> 00:17:44,214
we create the society in which we live.

317
00:17:44,234 --> 00:17:51,214
Out of that relationship all our existence comes.

318
00:17:51,234 --> 00:17:55,214
This would take us back again to the earlier statement,

319
00:17:55,234 --> 00:17:57,214
I am the world and the world is me.

320
00:17:57,234 --> 00:17:58,214
Yes, sir.

321
00:17:58,234 --> 00:18:02,214
That is a statement about relationship.

322
00:18:02,234 --> 00:18:04,214
It's a statement about many other things too.

323
00:18:04,234 --> 00:18:05,214
Of course.

324
00:18:05,234 --> 00:18:07,214
But that is a statement about relationship.

325
00:18:07,234 --> 00:18:11,214
The statement, the description is not the described,

326
00:18:11,234 --> 00:18:14,214
is the statement of the rupture

327
00:18:14,234 --> 00:18:15,214
of the relationship.

328
00:18:15,234 --> 00:18:16,214
That's right.

329
00:18:16,234 --> 00:18:19,214
In terms of everyday activity.

330
00:18:19,234 --> 00:18:23,214
Sir, everyday activity is my life, is our life.

331
00:18:23,234 --> 00:18:25,214
Is everything. Yes, precisely.

332
00:18:25,234 --> 00:18:27,214
Whether I go to the office, factory,

333
00:18:27,234 --> 00:18:30,214
or drive a bus, or whatever it is,

334
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:32,214
it is life, living.

335
00:18:32,234 --> 00:18:34,214
But it is interesting, isn't it,

336
00:18:34,234 --> 00:18:41,214
that even when that rupture is undergone

337
00:18:41,234 --> 00:18:44,214
at a very destructive level,

338
00:18:44,234 --> 00:18:47,214
what we've called thought,

339
00:18:47,234 --> 00:18:50,214
in the context of our description of it and image,

340
00:18:50,234 --> 00:18:52,214
becomes itself, even distorted.

341
00:18:52,234 --> 00:18:54,214
Of course.

342
00:18:54,234 --> 00:18:58,214
So that the distortion that we've been calling knowledge,

343
00:18:58,234 --> 00:19:00,214
in terms of its application,

344
00:19:00,234 --> 00:19:01,214
not what you described as

345
00:19:01,234 --> 00:19:02,224
I need to know how

346
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:03,214
to get from here to there.

347
00:19:03,234 --> 00:19:05,214
No, of course.

348
00:19:05,234 --> 00:19:11,214
Can itself suffer an even worse condition

349
00:19:11,234 --> 00:19:13,214
than we are presently related to?

350
00:19:13,234 --> 00:19:15,214
And we have tomes upon tomes

351
00:19:15,234 --> 00:19:17,214
about that pathology in itself, don't we?

352
00:19:17,234 --> 00:19:21,214
Yes, please do go on.

353
00:19:21,234 --> 00:19:25,214
So, knowledge and freedom.

354
00:19:25,234 --> 00:19:29,214
They must both exist together.

355
00:19:29,234 --> 00:19:32,214
Not freedom and knowledge.

356
00:19:32,234 --> 00:19:36,214
It's the harmony between the two.

357
00:19:36,234 --> 00:19:43,214
The two operating all the time in relationship.

358
00:19:43,234 --> 00:19:47,214
The knowledge and the freedom.

359
00:19:47,234 --> 00:19:48,214
Freedom.

360
00:19:48,234 --> 00:19:49,214
In harmony.

361
00:19:49,234 --> 00:19:50,214
In harmony.

362
00:19:50,234 --> 00:19:55,214
It's like they can never be divorced.

363
00:19:55,234 --> 00:19:59,214
If I want to live with you in great harmony,

364
00:19:59,234 --> 00:20:02,214
which is love,

365
00:20:02,234 --> 00:20:06,214
which we will discuss that later on,

366
00:20:06,234 --> 00:20:13,214
there must be this absolute sense of freedom from you,

367
00:20:13,234 --> 00:20:16,214
not dependency and so on, so on, so on.

368
00:20:16,234 --> 00:20:19,214
This absolute sense of freedom,

369
00:20:19,234 --> 00:20:21,724
and operating at the same

370
00:20:21,724 --> 00:20:24,214
time in the field of knowledge.

371
00:20:24,234 --> 00:20:27,214
Exactly.

372
00:20:27,234 --> 00:20:34,214
So somehow this knowledge,

373
00:20:34,234 --> 00:20:37,214
if I may use a theological word here

374
00:20:37,234 --> 00:20:41,214
without prejudicing what we are talking about,

375
00:20:41,234 --> 00:20:43,214
if in correct relationship

376
00:20:43,234 --> 00:20:45,214
with this freedom,

377
00:20:45,234 --> 00:20:49,214
is somehow continuously redeemed.

378
00:20:49,234 --> 00:20:53,214
It is somehow operating no longer destructively,

379
00:20:53,234 --> 00:20:57,214
but in coordination with the freedom

380
00:20:57,234 --> 00:21:01,214
in which I may live,

381
00:21:01,234 --> 00:21:03,214
because we haven't got to that freedom yet.

382
00:21:03,234 --> 00:21:09,214
No, that's why we have somewhat analysed

383
00:21:09,234 --> 00:21:13,214
or discussed or opened the question of knowledge.

384
00:21:13,234 --> 00:21:14,214
Yes.

385
00:21:14,234 --> 00:21:16,214
And we haven't gone into the question of freedom,

386
00:21:16,234 --> 00:21:18,214
what it means.

387
00:21:18,234 --> 00:21:20,214
No, but we have established something, I think,

388
00:21:20,234 --> 00:21:27,214
that this conversation so far has revealed,

389
00:21:27,234 --> 00:21:30,214
which is terribly important,

390
00:21:30,234 --> 00:21:32,214
at least I'd say for my students,

391
00:21:32,234 --> 00:21:37,214
in terms of helping them

392
00:21:37,234 --> 00:21:39,214
not to misunderstand what you are saying.

393
00:21:39,234 --> 00:21:40,214
Quite.

394
00:21:40,234 --> 00:21:42,214
I have the feeling that many persons,

395
00:21:42,234 --> 00:21:46,214
if they are not sufficiently attentive to what you say,

396
00:21:46,234 --> 00:21:51,214
simply dismiss many statements you say out of hand as...

397
00:21:51,234 --> 00:21:52,214
Impossible.

398
00:21:52,234 --> 00:21:54,214
...as either impossible,

399
00:21:54,234 --> 00:21:58,214
or if they like the aesthetics of it,

400
00:21:58,234 --> 00:22:00,214
it still doesn't apply to them.

401
00:22:00,234 --> 00:22:02,214
It's a lovely thing out there.

402
00:22:02,234 --> 00:22:05,214
Wouldn't it be great if somehow we could do this?

403
00:22:05,234 --> 00:22:06,214
Yes, quite.

404
00:22:06,234 --> 00:22:07,214
But you see, you haven't said that.

405
00:22:07,234 --> 00:22:09,214
You haven't said what they think you've said.

406
00:22:09,234 --> 00:22:12,214
You've said something about knowledge,

407
00:22:12,234 --> 00:22:14,214
with respect to pathology,

408
00:22:14,234 --> 00:22:16,214
and you've said something about knowledge,

409
00:22:16,234 --> 00:22:21,214
in which knowledge itself is no longer destructive.

410
00:22:21,234 --> 00:22:22,214
No.

411
00:22:22,234 --> 00:22:24,724
So we are not saying that

412
00:22:24,724 --> 00:22:27,214
knowledge as such is the bad guy,

413
00:22:27,234 --> 00:22:29,214
and something else is the good guy.

414
00:22:29,234 --> 00:22:30,214
No.

415
00:22:30,234 --> 00:22:33,214
No, I think it's terribly important that that's seen.

416
00:22:33,234 --> 00:22:34,214
Yes, that's what I...

417
00:22:34,234 --> 00:22:36,214
I wouldn't mind it being repeated over and over again.

418
00:22:36,234 --> 00:22:38,214
Quite, quite.

419
00:22:38,234 --> 00:22:42,214
Because I do heartily feel

420
00:22:42,234 --> 00:22:44,214
that it's easy to misunderstand it here.

421
00:22:44,234 --> 00:22:49,214
You see, sir, that's very important because religion,

422
00:22:49,234 --> 00:22:51,214
at least the meaning of that word,

423
00:22:51,234 --> 00:22:57,214
is to gather together to be attentive.

424
00:22:57,234 --> 00:23:01,214
That is the true meaning of that word, religion.

425
00:23:01,234 --> 00:23:02,214
I've looked it up...

426
00:23:02,234 --> 00:23:04,214
Oh, yes, I agree.

427
00:23:04,234 --> 00:23:09,214
Gathering together all energy to be attentive.

428
00:23:09,234 --> 00:23:11,214
Yes, to be attentive.

429
00:23:11,234 --> 00:23:14,214
Otherwise it's not religion.

430
00:23:14,234 --> 00:23:16,214
Religion is all the thing...

431
00:23:16,234 --> 00:23:19,214
So, we'll discuss that when you come to it.

432
00:23:19,234 --> 00:23:29,214
So, freedom means the sense of complete austerity

433
00:23:29,234 --> 00:23:35,214
and sense of total negation of the observer.

434
00:23:35,234 --> 00:23:39,214
Exactly.

435
00:23:39,234 --> 00:23:41,214
Out of that comes

436
00:23:41,234 --> 00:23:44,214
ignorance, austerity, everything else.

437
00:23:44,234 --> 00:23:46,214
We'll go into that later on.

438
00:23:46,234 --> 00:23:49,214
But austerity in itself doesn't produce it.

439
00:23:49,234 --> 00:23:50,214
No.

440
00:23:50,234 --> 00:23:52,214
We've turned that upside down.

441
00:23:52,234 --> 00:23:53,214
Right.

442
00:23:53,234 --> 00:23:58,214
Austere means, really, the word itself means ash.

443
00:23:58,234 --> 00:23:59,214
Yes.

444
00:23:59,234 --> 00:24:03,214
Dry, brittle.

445
00:24:03,234 --> 00:24:06,214
But the austerity of which we're talking about

446
00:24:06,234 --> 00:24:08,214
is something entirely different.

447
00:24:08,234 --> 00:24:11,214
It is the freedom

448
00:24:11,234 --> 00:24:13,214
of this austerity, inwardly.

449
00:24:13,234 --> 00:24:18,214
There's a beautiful biblical phrase that points to this.

450
00:24:18,234 --> 00:24:22,214
Just three words, beauty for ashes.

451
00:24:22,234 --> 00:24:25,214
When a transformation takes place.

452
00:24:25,234 --> 00:24:26,724
And in English we have

453
00:24:26,724 --> 00:24:28,214
the phrase, ashes in the mouth.

454
00:24:28,234 --> 00:24:31,214
When the whole thing has come to the earth.

455
00:24:31,234 --> 00:24:33,214
Come, ashes in the mouth.

456
00:24:33,234 --> 00:24:36,214
But there's the change from ashes to beauty.

457
00:24:36,234 --> 00:24:47,214
So, freedom in action in the field of knowledge.

458
00:24:47,234 --> 00:24:52,214
And in the field of human relationship.

459
00:24:52,234 --> 00:24:57,214
Because that is the highest importance, human relationship.

460
00:24:57,234 --> 00:24:59,214
Oh yes, yes.

461
00:24:59,234 --> 00:25:00,724
Oh yes, particularly if I am

462
00:25:00,724 --> 00:25:02,214
the world and the world is me.

463
00:25:02,234 --> 00:25:04,214
Obviously.

464
00:25:04,234 --> 00:25:05,214
Yes.

465
00:25:05,214 --> 00:25:14,214
So, what place has knowledge in human relationship?

466
00:25:14,234 --> 00:25:21,214
Knowledge in the sense, past experience, tradition, image.

467
00:25:21,234 --> 00:25:23,214
Yes.

468
00:25:23,234 --> 00:25:26,214
What has the observer, who is the observer,

469
00:25:26,234 --> 00:25:28,214
all that is the observer,

470
00:25:28,234 --> 00:25:34,214
what place has the observer in human relationship?

471
00:25:34,214 --> 00:25:36,214
What place has knowledge, on the one hand,

472
00:25:36,234 --> 00:25:38,214
what place has the observer?

473
00:25:38,234 --> 00:25:40,214
Observer is the knowledge.

474
00:25:40,234 --> 00:25:41,214
Is the knowledge.

475
00:25:41,234 --> 00:25:46,214
But there's the possibility of seeing knowledge,

476
00:25:46,234 --> 00:25:49,214
not simply negatively,

477
00:25:49,234 --> 00:25:53,214
but in coordination, in true creative relationship.

478
00:25:53,234 --> 00:25:55,214
I said that.

479
00:25:55,234 --> 00:25:56,214
Exactly.

480
00:25:56,234 --> 00:25:59,214
That is, I am related to you.

481
00:25:59,234 --> 00:26:02,234
Let's... to make it very simple.

482
00:26:02,254 --> 00:26:04,214
I am related to you.

483
00:26:04,234 --> 00:26:06,214
You are my brother, or whatever it is,

484
00:26:06,234 --> 00:26:09,214
husband, wife, whatever it is.

485
00:26:09,234 --> 00:26:16,214
And what place has knowledge as the observer,

486
00:26:16,234 --> 00:26:22,214
which is the past, and knowledge is the past,

487
00:26:22,234 --> 00:26:28,214
what place has that in our relationship?

488
00:26:28,234 --> 00:26:33,214
If our relationship is creative, in the sense...

489
00:26:33,234 --> 00:26:35,214
And it is not.

490
00:26:35,234 --> 00:26:37,214
Not if.

491
00:26:37,234 --> 00:26:41,214
We must take it actually as it is.

492
00:26:41,234 --> 00:26:44,214
I am related to you, I am married to you,

493
00:26:44,234 --> 00:26:48,214
I am your wife or husband, whatever it is.

494
00:26:48,234 --> 00:26:52,214
Now, what is the actuality in that relationship?

495
00:26:52,234 --> 00:26:56,214
The actuality, not theoretical actuality,

496
00:26:56,234 --> 00:27:00,214
but the actuality is that I am separate from you.

497
00:27:00,234 --> 00:27:03,214
The actuality must be that we are not divided.

498
00:27:03,234 --> 00:27:06,214
We are.

499
00:27:06,234 --> 00:27:09,214
I may call you my husband, my wife,

500
00:27:09,234 --> 00:27:13,214
but I am concerned with my success,

501
00:27:13,234 --> 00:27:15,214
I am concerned with my money,

502
00:27:15,234 --> 00:27:20,214
I am concerned with my ambitions, my envy,

503
00:27:20,234 --> 00:27:23,214
I am full of me.

504
00:27:23,234 --> 00:27:24,214
Yes, I see that.

505
00:27:24,234 --> 00:27:28,214
But I want to make sure now that

506
00:27:29,234 --> 00:27:31,214
we haven't reached a confusion here.

507
00:27:31,234 --> 00:27:32,214
Yes, we have.

508
00:27:32,214 --> 00:27:35,214
When I say that the actuality

509
00:27:35,214 --> 00:27:38,214
is that we are not separate,

510
00:27:38,234 --> 00:27:43,214
I don't mean to say that at the phenomenal level

511
00:27:43,234 --> 00:27:45,214
that a dysfunction is occurring.

512
00:27:45,234 --> 00:27:47,214
I am fully aware of that.

513
00:27:47,234 --> 00:27:48,224
But if we are going to

514
00:27:48,224 --> 00:27:49,214
say that the world is me

515
00:27:49,234 --> 00:27:50,214
and I am the world...

516
00:27:50,234 --> 00:27:53,214
Ah, we say it theoretically, we don't feel it.

517
00:27:53,234 --> 00:27:54,214
Precisely.

518
00:27:54,234 --> 00:27:56,224
But if that is the

519
00:27:56,224 --> 00:27:58,214
case, that the world is me

520
00:27:58,234 --> 00:28:01,214
and I am the world...

521
00:28:01,214 --> 00:28:04,214
And this is actual. This is actual.

522
00:28:04,234 --> 00:28:06,224
This is actual only when

523
00:28:06,224 --> 00:28:08,214
I have no division in myself.

524
00:28:08,234 --> 00:28:09,214
Exactly.

525
00:28:09,234 --> 00:28:11,214
But I have a division.

526
00:28:11,234 --> 00:28:12,214
If I have a division...

527
00:28:12,234 --> 00:28:13,214
And therefore it is just...

528
00:28:13,234 --> 00:28:16,214
...then there is no relationship between one and the other.

529
00:28:16,234 --> 00:28:23,214
Therefore, one accepts the idea

530
00:28:23,234 --> 00:28:25,724
that the world is me and

531
00:28:25,724 --> 00:28:28,214
the world, me is the world.

532
00:28:28,234 --> 00:28:31,214
That is just an idea.

533
00:28:31,234 --> 00:28:32,214
Look, sir...

534
00:28:32,234 --> 00:28:35,214
Yes, I understand, but if and when it happens...

535
00:28:35,234 --> 00:28:37,214
No, wait. Just see what takes place in my mind,

536
00:28:37,234 --> 00:28:39,214
what takes place in my mind.

537
00:28:39,234 --> 00:28:41,214
I make a statement of that kind,

538
00:28:41,234 --> 00:28:44,214
the world is you and you are the world.

539
00:28:44,234 --> 00:28:50,214
The mind then translates it into an idea,

540
00:28:50,234 --> 00:28:53,214
into a concept,

541
00:28:53,234 --> 00:28:56,214
and tries to live according to that concept.

542
00:28:56,234 --> 00:28:57,214
Exactly.

543
00:28:57,234 --> 00:29:01,214
It has abstracted from reality.

544
00:29:01,234 --> 00:29:08,214
This is knowledge in the destructive sense.

545
00:29:08,234 --> 00:29:10,214
That is what is going on.

546
00:29:10,234 --> 00:29:12,214
I won't call it destructive or positive.

547
00:29:12,234 --> 00:29:14,214
This is what is going on.

548
00:29:14,234 --> 00:29:17,214
Well, let's say the issue from it is hell.

549
00:29:17,234 --> 00:29:19,214
Yes, yes.

550
00:29:19,234 --> 00:29:25,214
So, in my relationship with you,

551
00:29:25,234 --> 00:29:30,214
what place has knowledge, the past, the image,

552
00:29:30,234 --> 00:29:34,214
which is the observer, all that is the observer,

553
00:29:34,234 --> 00:29:39,214
what place has the observer in our relationship?

554
00:29:39,234 --> 00:29:44,214
Actually, the observer is the factor of division.

555
00:29:44,234 --> 00:29:46,214
Right.

556
00:29:46,234 --> 00:29:49,214
And therefore, the conflict between you and me,

557
00:29:49,234 --> 00:29:51,224
this is what is going

558
00:29:51,224 --> 00:29:53,214
on in the world, every day.

559
00:29:53,234 --> 00:29:56,214
Then one would have to say, it seems to me,

560
00:29:56,234 --> 00:29:59,214
following the conversation,

561
00:29:59,214 --> 00:30:01,214
point by point,

562
00:30:01,234 --> 00:30:04,214
that the place of this observer,

563
00:30:04,234 --> 00:30:07,214
understood as you have pointed it out,

564
00:30:07,234 --> 00:30:13,214
is the point of this relationship.

565
00:30:13,234 --> 00:30:17,214
It is the point where there is really, actually,

566
00:30:17,234 --> 00:30:19,214
no relationship at all.

567
00:30:19,234 --> 00:30:22,214
I may sleep with my wife, or you may sleep,

568
00:30:22,234 --> 00:30:23,214
and so on, so on,

569
00:30:23,234 --> 00:30:27,214
but actually there is no relationship.

570
00:30:27,234 --> 00:30:29,214
Uh-huh.

571
00:30:29,234 --> 00:30:34,214
Because I have my own pursuits, my own ambitions,

572
00:30:34,234 --> 00:30:36,214
all the idiosyncrasies, and so on,

573
00:30:36,234 --> 00:30:39,214
and she has hers.

574
00:30:39,234 --> 00:30:44,214
So we are always separate.

575
00:30:44,234 --> 00:30:50,214
And therefore always in battle with each other.

576
00:30:50,234 --> 00:30:54,214
Which means the observer as the past

577
00:30:54,234 --> 00:30:57,214
is the factor of division.

578
00:30:57,234 --> 00:30:59,214
Yes.

579
00:30:59,234 --> 00:31:02,214
I was just wanting to be sure that the phrase,

580
00:31:02,234 --> 00:31:04,214
is the place,

581
00:31:04,234 --> 00:31:06,214
what is the place of the observer,

582
00:31:06,234 --> 00:31:09,214
was understood in the context of what we are saying.

583
00:31:09,234 --> 00:31:10,724
We have made the statement

584
00:31:10,724 --> 00:31:12,214
that there is such a thing.

585
00:31:12,234 --> 00:31:13,214
Yes.

586
00:31:13,234 --> 00:31:17,214
Well, its place as such would seem to me

587
00:31:17,234 --> 00:31:19,724
not to be what we usually

588
00:31:19,724 --> 00:31:22,214
mean by its occupying a place.

589
00:31:22,234 --> 00:31:23,214
Yes.

590
00:31:23,234 --> 00:31:27,214
We are talking rather about an activity here

591
00:31:27,234 --> 00:31:30,214
that is profoundly disordered.

592
00:31:30,234 --> 00:31:35,214
Sir, as long as there is the observer,

593
00:31:35,234 --> 00:31:39,214
there must be conflict in relationship.

594
00:31:39,234 --> 00:31:40,214
Yes, I follow that.

595
00:31:40,234 --> 00:31:41,214
Wait, wait.

596
00:31:41,234 --> 00:31:43,214
No, see what happens.

597
00:31:43,234 --> 00:31:45,214
I make a statement of that kind.

598
00:31:45,234 --> 00:31:48,214
Someone will translate into an idea,

599
00:31:48,234 --> 00:31:50,214
into a concept,

600
00:31:50,234 --> 00:31:54,214
and say, how am I to live that concept?

601
00:31:54,214 --> 00:32:02,214
The fact is he doesn't observe himself as the observer.

602
00:32:02,234 --> 00:32:04,214
That's right.

603
00:32:04,234 --> 00:32:05,214
That's right.

604
00:32:05,234 --> 00:32:07,214
He is the observer looking out there,

605
00:32:07,234 --> 00:32:09,214
making a distinction between himself...

606
00:32:09,234 --> 00:32:11,214
And the statement.

607
00:32:11,234 --> 00:32:13,214
Right, making a division.

608
00:32:13,234 --> 00:32:14,214
Division.

609
00:32:14,234 --> 00:32:18,224
Now, so, has the observer

610
00:32:18,224 --> 00:32:22,214
any place at all in relationship?

611
00:32:22,234 --> 00:32:23,214
I say...

612
00:32:23,214 --> 00:32:24,214
I say no.

613
00:32:24,234 --> 00:32:28,214
The moment he comes into existence,

614
00:32:28,234 --> 00:32:34,214
into relationship, there is no relationship.

615
00:32:34,234 --> 00:32:37,214
The relationship is not...

616
00:32:37,234 --> 00:32:38,214
Is not. That's right.

617
00:32:38,234 --> 00:32:42,214
...is not something that is in dis-relationship.

618
00:32:42,234 --> 00:32:43,214
Yes, that's right.

619
00:32:43,234 --> 00:32:44,724
We are talking about something that

620
00:32:44,724 --> 00:32:46,214
in fact does not even exist.

621
00:32:46,234 --> 00:32:48,214
Exists.

622
00:32:48,234 --> 00:32:52,214
Therefore we have to go into the question

623
00:32:52,214 --> 00:32:56,214
why human beings in their relationship

624
00:32:56,234 --> 00:33:00,214
with other human beings are so violent.

625
00:33:00,234 --> 00:33:05,214
Because that is spreading throughout the world.

626
00:33:05,234 --> 00:33:08,214
I was told the other day in India,

627
00:33:08,234 --> 00:33:11,214
a mother came to see me,

628
00:33:11,234 --> 00:33:14,224
very brahmanical family and very cultured

629
00:33:14,224 --> 00:33:17,214
and all the rest of it.

630
00:33:17,234 --> 00:33:20,234
Her son, who is six,

631
00:33:20,254 --> 00:33:22,194
when she asked him to do something,

632
00:33:22,194 --> 00:33:25,194
he took up a stick and began to hit her.

633
00:33:25,214 --> 00:33:29,194
A thing unknown. You follow, sir?

634
00:33:29,214 --> 00:33:34,194
I mean, the idea that you should hit your mother

635
00:33:34,214 --> 00:33:38,194
is traditionally something incredible.

636
00:33:38,214 --> 00:33:41,194
And this boy did it.

637
00:33:41,214 --> 00:33:45,194
And I said, see what is the fact.

638
00:33:45,214 --> 00:33:48,194
We went into it, she understood, so on.

639
00:33:48,214 --> 00:33:52,194
So, to understand violence, one has to understand violence.

640
00:33:52,214 --> 00:33:57,194
One has to understand division.

641
00:33:57,214 --> 00:33:59,194
The division was already there.

642
00:33:59,214 --> 00:34:02,194
Otherwise he would not have picked up the stick.

643
00:34:02,214 --> 00:34:07,194
Division between nations. You follow, sir?

644
00:34:07,214 --> 00:34:10,204
This race form armaments is

645
00:34:10,204 --> 00:34:13,194
one of the factors of violence,

646
00:34:13,214 --> 00:34:17,194
which is, I am calling myself American,

647
00:34:17,214 --> 00:34:18,704
and others calling himself Russian

648
00:34:18,704 --> 00:34:20,194
or Hindu or whatever it is,

649
00:34:20,214 --> 00:34:27,194
this division is the factor of real violence and hatred.

650
00:34:27,214 --> 00:34:30,194
If a mind... not if a...

651
00:34:30,214 --> 00:34:32,704
When a mind sees that, he

652
00:34:32,704 --> 00:34:35,194
cuts away all division in himself.

653
00:34:35,214 --> 00:34:38,194
He is no longer a Hindu, American, Russian,

654
00:34:38,214 --> 00:34:41,194
he is a human being,

655
00:34:41,214 --> 00:34:45,194
with his problems, which then he is trying to solve,

656
00:34:45,214 --> 00:34:50,194
not in terms of India or America or Russia.

657
00:34:50,214 --> 00:34:53,194
So that's...

658
00:34:53,214 --> 00:34:56,194
So we come to the point,

659
00:34:56,214 --> 00:35:04,194
can the mind be free in the relationship,

660
00:35:04,214 --> 00:35:08,194
which means orderly, not chaotic.

661
00:35:08,214 --> 00:35:12,194
No, no. Orderly.

662
00:35:12,214 --> 00:35:13,704
It has to be, otherwise

663
00:35:13,704 --> 00:35:15,194
you couldn't use the word relation.

664
00:35:15,214 --> 00:35:20,194
No, no. So can the mind be free of that?

665
00:35:20,214 --> 00:35:25,194
Free of the observer.

666
00:35:25,214 --> 00:35:27,194
If not, there is no hope.

667
00:35:27,214 --> 00:35:29,194
That's the whole point.

668
00:35:29,214 --> 00:35:31,194
If not, we've had it.

669
00:35:31,214 --> 00:35:35,194
And all the escapes and going off into other religions,

670
00:35:35,214 --> 00:35:39,194
doing all kinds of tricks, and no meaning.

671
00:35:39,214 --> 00:35:46,194
Now, this demands a great deal of perception, insight,

672
00:35:46,214 --> 00:35:50,194
into the fact of your life,

673
00:35:50,214 --> 00:35:53,194
how one lives one's life.

674
00:35:53,214 --> 00:35:57,194
After all, philosophy means the love of truth,

675
00:35:57,214 --> 00:35:59,194
love of wisdom,

676
00:35:59,214 --> 00:36:02,194
not the love of some abstraction.

677
00:36:02,214 --> 00:36:05,194
Oh, no. Oh, no, no, no.

678
00:36:05,214 --> 00:36:07,194
Wisdom is supremely practical.

679
00:36:07,214 --> 00:36:10,194
Practical. Therefore, here it is.

680
00:36:10,214 --> 00:36:17,194
That is, can a human being live in relationship,

681
00:36:17,214 --> 00:36:19,194
in freedom,

682
00:36:19,214 --> 00:36:24,194
and yet operate in the field of knowledge?

683
00:36:24,214 --> 00:36:27,194
And yet operate in the field of knowledge.

684
00:36:27,214 --> 00:36:34,194
And be absolutely orderly.

685
00:36:34,214 --> 00:36:37,194
Otherwise it's not freedom.

686
00:36:37,214 --> 00:36:40,194
Because order means virtue.

687
00:36:40,214 --> 00:36:43,194
Yes. Yes.

688
00:36:43,214 --> 00:36:46,194
Which doesn't exist in the world at the present time.

689
00:36:46,194 --> 00:36:50,194
There is no sense of virtue in anything.

690
00:36:50,214 --> 00:36:52,194
They will repeat,

691
00:36:52,214 --> 00:36:54,194
virtue is a creative thing,

692
00:36:54,214 --> 00:36:58,194
is a living thing, is a moving thing.

693
00:36:58,214 --> 00:37:05,194
I'm thinking, as you're saying this, about virtue,

694
00:37:05,214 --> 00:37:08,194
which is really power,

695
00:37:08,214 --> 00:37:13,194
which is really the ability to act.

696
00:37:13,214 --> 00:37:16,194
And if I'm following you correctly,

697
00:37:16,214 --> 00:37:20,194
what you're really saying,

698
00:37:20,214 --> 00:37:23,194
and please correct me if I'm way off here,

699
00:37:23,214 --> 00:37:27,194
what you're really saying is that

700
00:37:27,214 --> 00:37:35,194
the ability to act in the strict sense,

701
00:37:35,214 --> 00:37:38,194
which must be creative,

702
00:37:38,214 --> 00:37:41,194
otherwise it's not an action,

703
00:37:41,214 --> 00:37:43,194
but it is simply a reaction.

704
00:37:43,214 --> 00:37:46,194
Yes, a repetition. A repetition.

705
00:37:46,214 --> 00:37:49,704
That the ability to act,

706
00:37:49,704 --> 00:37:53,194
or virtue, as you put it,

707
00:37:53,214 --> 00:37:57,194
bears with it, necessarily,

708
00:37:57,214 --> 00:38:00,194
the implication of order.

709
00:38:00,214 --> 00:38:02,194
It must.

710
00:38:02,214 --> 00:38:05,194
There seems to me no way out of that.

711
00:38:05,214 --> 00:38:06,194
Yes. Yes.

712
00:38:06,214 --> 00:38:09,194
I just wanted to recover that step at a time.

713
00:38:09,214 --> 00:38:12,194
So can I come back?

714
00:38:12,214 --> 00:38:13,194
Yes.

715
00:38:13,214 --> 00:38:20,194
In human relationship as it exists now,

716
00:38:20,214 --> 00:38:24,194
we are looking at that, what actually is.

717
00:38:24,214 --> 00:38:29,194
In that human relationship there is conflict,

718
00:38:29,214 --> 00:38:33,194
sexual violence and so on, so on, so on,

719
00:38:33,214 --> 00:38:36,194
every kind of violence.

720
00:38:36,214 --> 00:38:42,194
Now, can man live at total peace

721
00:38:42,214 --> 00:38:47,194
otherwise it's not creative?

722
00:38:47,214 --> 00:38:49,194
In human relationship,

723
00:38:49,214 --> 00:38:53,194
because that is the basis of all life.

724
00:38:53,214 --> 00:38:55,194
You understand?

725
00:38:55,214 --> 00:39:01,194
I'm very taken with the way you have pursued this.

726
00:39:01,214 --> 00:39:05,194
I notice that when we ask this question,

727
00:39:05,214 --> 00:39:09,194
is it possible that,

728
00:39:09,214 --> 00:39:12,194
the reference for it is always a totality.

729
00:39:12,214 --> 00:39:14,194
Yes.

730
00:39:14,214 --> 00:39:18,194
And the reference over here is a fragment,

731
00:39:18,214 --> 00:39:22,194
or a fragmentation, or a division.

732
00:39:22,214 --> 00:39:25,204
Never once have you said that

733
00:39:25,204 --> 00:39:28,194
the passage from one to the other

734
00:39:28,214 --> 00:39:32,194
is a movement that even exists.

735
00:39:32,214 --> 00:39:33,194
No, it can't exist.

736
00:39:33,214 --> 00:39:36,194
Quite quite. Absolutely.

737
00:39:36,214 --> 00:39:39,204
I think, Mr Krishnamurti, that

738
00:39:39,204 --> 00:39:42,194
nothing is so difficult to grasp.

739
00:39:42,214 --> 00:39:44,194
As this statement that you have made.

740
00:39:44,214 --> 00:39:46,194
From this to that.

741
00:39:46,214 --> 00:39:49,194
Yes.

742
00:39:49,214 --> 00:39:55,194
There is nothing that we are taught from childhood up

743
00:39:55,214 --> 00:40:03,194
to render such a possibility,

744
00:40:03,214 --> 00:40:07,194
a matter, for taking seriously.

745
00:40:07,214 --> 00:40:10,194
Because, well, of course,

746
00:40:10,214 --> 00:40:13,194
one doesn't like to make sweeping statements

747
00:40:13,214 --> 00:40:15,194
about the way everybody has been educated.

748
00:40:15,214 --> 00:40:17,194
But I'm thinking of myself,

749
00:40:17,214 --> 00:40:22,194
from a child upward,

750
00:40:22,214 --> 00:40:27,194
all the way through graduate school,

751
00:40:27,214 --> 00:40:29,194
accumulating a lot of this knowledge

752
00:40:29,214 --> 00:40:34,194
that you have been talking about.

753
00:40:34,214 --> 00:40:40,194
I don't remember anybody saying to me,

754
00:40:40,214 --> 00:40:44,194
you know, you've been pointing me to a literature

755
00:40:44,214 --> 00:40:48,194
that so categorically makes this distinction

756
00:40:48,214 --> 00:40:52,704
between one and the other

757
00:40:52,704 --> 00:40:57,194
as in terms of each other,

758
00:40:57,214 --> 00:41:00,194
not accessible to each other through passage.

759
00:41:00,214 --> 00:41:03,194
No, no, no. Quite, quite.

760
00:41:03,214 --> 00:41:06,194
Now, I'm correct in understanding you, aren't I?

761
00:41:06,214 --> 00:41:08,194
Quite right.

762
00:41:08,214 --> 00:41:10,194
Maybe I could just say this

763
00:41:10,214 --> 00:41:11,194
as an aside.

764
00:41:11,214 --> 00:41:13,194
The fragment can't become the whole.

765
00:41:13,214 --> 00:41:15,194
No, the fragment cannot become the whole,

766
00:41:15,214 --> 00:41:16,194
in and of itself.

767
00:41:16,214 --> 00:41:19,194
But the fragment is always trying to become the whole.

768
00:41:19,214 --> 00:41:23,194
Exactly, exactly.

769
00:41:23,214 --> 00:41:30,194
Now, of course, in the years of very serious

770
00:41:30,214 --> 00:41:35,194
and devoted contemplation and exploration of this,

771
00:41:35,214 --> 00:41:38,194
which quite clearly you have undertaken

772
00:41:38,214 --> 00:41:40,194
with great passion,

773
00:41:40,214 --> 00:41:44,194
I suppose it must have occurred to you

774
00:41:44,214 --> 00:41:48,194
that the first sight of this,

775
00:41:48,214 --> 00:41:53,194
while one is in a condition of the observer,

776
00:41:53,214 --> 00:41:55,194
must be very frightening.

777
00:41:55,214 --> 00:41:57,194
In the condition of the observer,

778
00:41:57,214 --> 00:41:59,194
the thought that there is no passage.

779
00:41:59,214 --> 00:42:01,704
No, but you see, I

780
00:42:01,704 --> 00:42:04,194
never looked at it that way.

781
00:42:04,214 --> 00:42:06,194
But please tell me how you looked at it.

782
00:42:06,214 --> 00:42:08,194
Please.

783
00:42:10,214 --> 00:42:17,194
From childhood I never thought I was a Hindu.

784
00:42:17,214 --> 00:42:18,194
I see.

785
00:42:18,214 --> 00:42:21,194
I never thought when I was educated in England

786
00:42:21,214 --> 00:42:24,194
and all the rest of it, that I was European.

787
00:42:24,214 --> 00:42:29,194
I just, I never was caught in that trap.

788
00:42:29,214 --> 00:42:30,194
I don't know how it happened.

789
00:42:30,214 --> 00:42:33,194
I was never caught in the trap.

790
00:42:33,214 --> 00:42:35,194
When you were quite little then,

791
00:42:35,214 --> 00:42:38,194
and your playmates said to you,

792
00:42:38,194 --> 00:42:40,194
well, now look, you are a Hindu,

793
00:42:40,214 --> 00:42:41,194
what did you say?

794
00:42:41,214 --> 00:42:43,194
I probably put on Hinduism,

795
00:42:43,214 --> 00:42:48,194
you know, all the trappings of Brahman tradition, I was.

796
00:42:48,214 --> 00:42:51,194
But it never penetrated deeply.

797
00:42:51,214 --> 00:42:52,704
As we say in the

798
00:42:52,704 --> 00:42:54,194
vernacular, it never got to you.

799
00:42:54,214 --> 00:42:56,194
It never got to me, that's right.

800
00:42:56,214 --> 00:42:58,194
I see. That's very remarkable.

801
00:42:58,214 --> 00:43:02,194
That is extraordinary.

802
00:43:02,214 --> 00:43:04,194
The vast number of people in the world

803
00:43:04,214 --> 00:43:07,194
seem to have been got to with respect to this.

804
00:43:07,194 --> 00:43:15,194
That's why I think, you see,

805
00:43:15,194 --> 00:43:26,194
propaganda has become the means of change.

806
00:43:26,214 --> 00:43:28,194
Yes, yes.

807
00:43:28,194 --> 00:43:33,194
Propaganda is not truth.

808
00:43:33,194 --> 00:43:36,194
Repetition is not truth.

809
00:43:36,194 --> 00:43:37,194
It's a formality.

810
00:43:37,214 --> 00:43:38,194
It's a form of violence too.

811
00:43:38,214 --> 00:43:40,194
That's just...

812
00:43:40,214 --> 00:43:41,194
Yes.

813
00:43:41,214 --> 00:43:46,194
So, a mind that merely observes,

814
00:43:46,214 --> 00:43:50,194
doesn't react to what it observes,

815
00:43:50,214 --> 00:43:53,194
according to its conditioning,

816
00:43:53,214 --> 00:43:58,194
which means there is no observer at any time,

817
00:43:58,214 --> 00:44:00,194
therefore no division.

818
00:44:00,214 --> 00:44:03,194
It happened to me,

819
00:44:03,214 --> 00:44:07,194
I don't know how it happened, but it's happened.

820
00:44:07,214 --> 00:44:11,194
In observing all this,

821
00:44:11,214 --> 00:44:14,194
I see in every human relationship,

822
00:44:14,214 --> 00:44:16,194
every kind of human relationship,

823
00:44:16,214 --> 00:44:20,194
there is this division and therefore violence.

824
00:44:20,214 --> 00:44:25,194
And to me the very essence of non-relationship

825
00:44:25,214 --> 00:44:31,194
is the factor of me and you.

826
00:44:31,214 --> 00:44:33,204
I was just trying to go

827
00:44:33,204 --> 00:44:35,194
back in my own personal history

828
00:44:35,214 --> 00:44:39,194
and think of when I was a child.

829
00:44:39,214 --> 00:44:45,194
I did, while accepting that I was different,

830
00:44:45,214 --> 00:44:47,194
I did believe that.

831
00:44:47,214 --> 00:44:49,194
I did come to accept that.

832
00:44:49,214 --> 00:44:51,194
There was something else, however,

833
00:44:51,214 --> 00:44:59,194
that always held me very, very hard to center

834
00:44:59,214 --> 00:45:03,194
in terms of making an ultimate issue of that.

835
00:45:03,214 --> 00:45:05,204
And that was an experience I

836
00:45:05,204 --> 00:45:07,194
had when I was rowing a boat.

837
00:45:07,214 --> 00:45:12,194
I spent some time in Scandinavia as a child,

838
00:45:12,214 --> 00:45:14,704
and I used to take the

839
00:45:14,704 --> 00:45:17,194
boat out on the fjord every day.

840
00:45:17,214 --> 00:45:20,194
And when I would row,

841
00:45:20,214 --> 00:45:27,194
I was profoundly moved by the action of the water

842
00:45:27,214 --> 00:45:30,194
when I moved the oar.

843
00:45:30,214 --> 00:45:33,194
Because I lifted the oar out of the water,

844
00:45:33,214 --> 00:45:37,194
and there was a separation in substance

845
00:45:37,214 --> 00:45:39,194
between the water and the oar.

846
00:45:39,214 --> 00:45:43,194
But the water, which was necessary for support

847
00:45:43,214 --> 00:45:50,194
and for purchase, so that I could propel myself,

848
00:45:50,214 --> 00:45:53,194
never lost touch with itself.

849
00:45:53,214 --> 00:45:57,194
It always turned into itself

850
00:45:57,214 --> 00:46:00,194
without ever having left itself in the beginning.

851
00:46:00,214 --> 00:46:03,194
And once in a while I would laugh at myself

852
00:46:03,214 --> 00:46:05,194
and say, if anyone catches you looking at this water

853
00:46:05,214 --> 00:46:07,194
any longer than you are doing,

854
00:46:07,214 --> 00:46:08,204
they will think that you

855
00:46:08,204 --> 00:46:09,194
are clear out of your mind.

856
00:46:09,214 --> 00:46:12,194
This is the observer talking to himself, of course.

857
00:46:12,214 --> 00:46:15,194
But that made such a profound impression on me

858
00:46:15,214 --> 00:46:19,194
that I think it was what you might call

859
00:46:19,214 --> 00:46:21,194
a little salvation for me.

860
00:46:21,214 --> 00:46:23,194
And I never lost that.

861
00:46:23,214 --> 00:46:26,194
So maybe there is some relationship

862
00:46:26,214 --> 00:46:28,194
between that apprehension,

863
00:46:28,214 --> 00:46:31,194
which I think changed my being,

864
00:46:31,214 --> 00:46:33,194
and what it is that you are talking about

865
00:46:33,214 --> 00:46:35,704
as one who never ever suffered

866
00:46:35,704 --> 00:46:38,194
this sense of separation at all.

867
00:46:38,214 --> 00:46:43,194
Yes. Yes. Please go ahead.

868
00:46:43,214 --> 00:46:48,194
So that brings us to the point, sir, doesn't it,

869
00:46:48,214 --> 00:46:51,194
can the human mind,

870
00:46:51,214 --> 00:46:56,194
which has evolved in separation...

871
00:46:56,214 --> 00:46:58,194
Yes.

872
00:46:58,214 --> 00:47:01,194
...in...

873
00:47:01,214 --> 00:47:03,194
...fragmentations...

874
00:47:03,214 --> 00:47:05,194
This is where evolution is. Yes.

875
00:47:05,214 --> 00:47:12,014
...can such a mind transform, undergo,

876
00:47:12,034 --> 00:47:13,314
ええ

877
00:47:13,314 --> 00:47:20,294
regeneration which is not produced by influence,

878
00:47:20,314 --> 00:47:28,874
by propaganda, by threat and punishment.

879
00:47:28,894 --> 00:47:31,504
Because if it changes because it

880
00:47:31,504 --> 00:47:34,114
is going to get a reward...

881
00:47:34,134 --> 00:47:36,714
It hasn't changed. It hasn't changed.

882
00:47:36,714 --> 00:47:41,434
So that is one of the fundamental things

883
00:47:41,434 --> 00:47:44,544
which one has to ask and

884
00:47:44,544 --> 00:47:47,654
answer it in action, not in words.

885
00:47:47,674 --> 00:47:48,994
In action. Action.

886
00:47:49,014 --> 00:47:50,554
Oh, yes, yes.

887
00:47:50,554 --> 00:47:58,854
Which is, my mind, the human mind,

888
00:47:58,874 --> 00:48:04,114
has evolved in contradiction, in duality,

889
00:48:04,114 --> 00:48:07,434
the me and the not-me,

890
00:48:07,434 --> 00:48:11,394
has evolved in this traditional

891
00:48:11,394 --> 00:48:16,513
cleavage, division, fragmentation.

892
00:48:16,513 --> 00:48:23,274
Now, can that mind observe this fact,

893
00:48:23,294 --> 00:48:28,154
observe without the observer,

894
00:48:28,154 --> 00:48:31,794
and only then there is a regeneration?

895
00:48:31,794 --> 00:48:35,474
As long as there is an observer observing this,

896
00:48:35,494 --> 00:48:36,724
then there is a conflict. I

897
00:48:36,724 --> 00:48:37,954
don't know if I am making...

898
00:48:37,954 --> 00:48:39,394
Yes, you do. You make

899
00:48:39,394 --> 00:48:40,834
yourself very clear on two levels.

900
00:48:40,834 --> 00:48:41,394
One is the mind.

901
00:48:41,414 --> 00:48:42,853
So, I made myself clear on two levels.

902
00:48:42,874 --> 00:48:44,493
On the level of discourse alone,

903
00:48:44,514 --> 00:48:46,014
which I know is not your major concern,

904
00:48:46,014 --> 00:48:49,894
on the level of discourse alone it necessarily follows

905
00:48:49,894 --> 00:48:55,814
that it must be the case that this possibility exists,

906
00:48:55,834 --> 00:48:58,514
otherwise we would be talking nonsense.

907
00:48:58,554 --> 00:49:06,494
But then the agony of the situation at large

908
00:49:06,494 --> 00:49:10,674
that we have been describing is simply that

909
00:49:10,674 --> 00:49:13,194
whether this can be done or

910
00:49:13,194 --> 00:49:15,714
no, never occurs to a person,

911
00:49:15,734 --> 00:49:20,674
and in the absence of it even occurring,

912
00:49:20,694 --> 00:49:24,394
the repetition is going to continue indefinitely

913
00:49:24,414 --> 00:49:27,054
and things are going to get worse and worse.

914
00:49:27,074 --> 00:49:33,294
Sir, the difficulty is most people won't even listen.

915
00:49:33,314 --> 00:49:38,134
I am sighing, I know that.

916
00:49:38,134 --> 00:49:41,834
Won't listen. If they do

917
00:49:41,834 --> 00:49:45,534
listen, they listen with their conclusions.

918
00:49:45,553 --> 00:49:48,143
If I am a communist, I will

919
00:49:48,143 --> 00:49:50,734
listen to you up to a point.

920
00:49:50,754 --> 00:49:54,534
After that I won't listen to you.

921
00:49:55,773 --> 00:50:00,734
And if I am slightly demented,

922
00:50:00,754 --> 00:50:04,574
I will listen to you and translate what I hear

923
00:50:04,594 --> 00:50:06,914
according to my...

924
00:50:06,934 --> 00:50:08,134
Dementia.

925
00:50:08,154 --> 00:50:09,234
Exactly.

926
00:50:09,254 --> 00:50:16,514
So, one has to be extraordinarily serious to listen.

927
00:50:16,534 --> 00:50:18,454
Serious in the sense,

928
00:50:18,474 --> 00:50:22,893
put aside my peculiar prejudices and idiosyncrasies

929
00:50:22,914 --> 00:50:26,494
and listen to what you are saying.

930
00:50:26,514 --> 00:50:34,194
Because the listening is the miracle,

931
00:50:34,214 --> 00:50:38,113
not what shall I do with what you have said.

932
00:50:38,154 --> 00:50:41,374
Not what shall I listen to.

933
00:50:41,393 --> 00:50:43,474
But the act of listening.

934
00:50:43,494 --> 00:50:48,514
The act of listening itself. We are back to ING.

935
00:50:48,534 --> 00:50:52,434
The listening itself.

936
00:50:52,454 --> 00:50:54,484
That requires... I mean, you are

937
00:50:54,484 --> 00:50:56,514
good enough to listen to me,

938
00:50:56,534 --> 00:50:58,514
because you want to find out.

939
00:50:58,534 --> 00:50:59,893
But the vast majority of people say,

940
00:50:59,914 --> 00:51:01,653
what are you talking about? I

941
00:51:01,653 --> 00:51:03,393
want to go and enjoy myself.

942
00:51:03,414 --> 00:51:06,314
So go and talk to somebody else.

943
00:51:06,333 --> 00:51:07,454
So,

944
00:51:07,454 --> 00:51:13,954
to create an atmosphere,

945
00:51:13,974 --> 00:51:17,173
to create an ambience, a feeling,

946
00:51:17,194 --> 00:51:22,773
look, life is dreadfully serious, my friend, do listen.

947
00:51:22,794 --> 00:51:26,493
It is your life, don't waste it, do listen.

948
00:51:26,514 --> 00:51:31,213
To bring about a human being that will listen

949
00:51:31,233 --> 00:51:34,634
is of the greatest importance,

950
00:51:34,653 --> 00:51:37,353
because we don't want to listen.

951
00:51:37,354 --> 00:51:40,814
It is too disturbing.

952
00:51:40,834 --> 00:51:42,234
I understand.

953
00:51:42,254 --> 00:51:45,724
I have tried sometimes in

954
00:51:45,724 --> 00:51:49,194
class to make this very point.

955
00:51:49,214 --> 00:51:56,294
And sometimes I suggest that we should watch the animal,

956
00:51:56,314 --> 00:51:58,594
especially the wild animal.

957
00:51:58,614 --> 00:51:59,954
Of course.

958
00:51:59,974 --> 00:52:03,594
Because if it is not listening, it is likely dead.

959
00:52:03,614 --> 00:52:04,974
Dead, yes, sir.

960
00:52:04,994 --> 00:52:07,014
There is this extraordinary,

961
00:52:07,014 --> 00:52:07,853
Attention.

962
00:52:07,874 --> 00:52:09,774
attention that it makes,

963
00:52:09,793 --> 00:52:16,514
and every instant of its life is a crisis.

964
00:52:16,533 --> 00:52:19,254
Ah, absolutely.

965
00:52:19,274 --> 00:52:21,254
And you know what happens?

966
00:52:21,274 --> 00:52:22,924
The eyes out there show in

967
00:52:22,924 --> 00:52:24,574
the main that they are thinking

968
00:52:24,594 --> 00:52:27,014
I am talking about animal psychology.

969
00:52:27,033 --> 00:52:29,254
I am not talking about psychology at all.

970
00:52:29,274 --> 00:52:32,014
I am talking about what is the case,

971
00:52:32,033 --> 00:52:33,254
which is either-or,

972
00:52:33,274 --> 00:52:34,914
and there isn't any way

973
00:52:34,914 --> 00:52:36,554
to get from either to or.

974
00:52:36,574 --> 00:52:36,794
Right.

975
00:52:36,794 --> 00:52:38,354
That's what I mean.

976
00:52:38,374 --> 00:52:40,354
So I think I understand you.

977
00:52:40,374 --> 00:52:44,274
You see, sir, in America what is happening is now,

978
00:52:44,294 --> 00:52:48,754
as I observe it, and I may be mistaken,

979
00:52:48,774 --> 00:52:51,794
they are not serious.

980
00:52:51,814 --> 00:52:56,714
They are playing with new things,

981
00:52:56,734 --> 00:52:59,974
something entertaining,

982
00:52:59,994 --> 00:53:02,594
go from one thing to the other.

983
00:53:02,614 --> 00:53:06,354
And they think this is searching.

984
00:53:06,354 --> 00:53:08,354
Searching.

985
00:53:08,374 --> 00:53:09,274
Yes.

986
00:53:09,294 --> 00:53:11,034
Searching, asking,

987
00:53:11,054 --> 00:53:14,354
but they get trapped in each one of them.

988
00:53:14,374 --> 00:53:15,234
Yes.

989
00:53:15,254 --> 00:53:17,504
And by the end of

990
00:53:17,504 --> 00:53:19,754
it they have nothing but ashes.

991
00:53:19,774 --> 00:53:23,634
So it is becoming more and more difficult

992
00:53:23,654 --> 00:53:28,114
for human beings to be serious,

993
00:53:28,134 --> 00:53:33,734
to listen, to see what they are,

994
00:53:33,754 --> 00:53:35,894
not what they should be.

995
00:53:35,894 --> 00:53:37,654
No, what is the case.

996
00:53:37,673 --> 00:53:38,494
What is.

997
00:53:38,514 --> 00:53:39,233
Exactly.

998
00:53:39,254 --> 00:53:48,654
That means you please do listen for five minutes.

999
00:53:48,674 --> 00:53:51,214
Uh-huh.

1000
00:53:51,233 --> 00:53:55,134
In this conversation you are listening,

1001
00:53:55,154 --> 00:53:56,443
because you are interested in

1002
00:53:56,443 --> 00:53:57,733
it, you want to find out.

1003
00:53:57,754 --> 00:53:59,533
But the vast majority of people, they say,

1004
00:53:59,554 --> 00:54:03,054
for God's sake, leave me alone,

1005
00:54:03,074 --> 00:54:05,674
I have my little house, my wife,

1006
00:54:05,674 --> 00:54:08,294
my car, my yacht, or whatever it is,

1007
00:54:08,314 --> 00:54:10,994
for God's sake, don't change

1008
00:54:10,994 --> 00:54:13,674
anything as long as I live.

1009
00:54:13,694 --> 00:54:16,564
You know, going back to

1010
00:54:16,564 --> 00:54:19,434
what I do know something about,

1011
00:54:19,454 --> 00:54:20,554
namely the academy,

1012
00:54:20,574 --> 00:54:27,554
because I am situated there in terms of day-to-day activity,

1013
00:54:27,574 --> 00:54:30,594
I have often remarked to myself in attending conferences,

1014
00:54:30,614 --> 00:54:34,814
where papers are read, that nobody is listening.

1015
00:54:34,834 --> 00:54:35,674
Ah.

1016
00:54:35,694 --> 00:54:37,054
Yes.

1017
00:54:37,074 --> 00:54:40,534
It's one long monologue,

1018
00:54:40,554 --> 00:54:42,434
and after a while you get the feeling

1019
00:54:42,454 --> 00:54:45,074
that it really is a shocking waste of time.

1020
00:54:45,094 --> 00:54:45,594
Yes.

1021
00:54:45,614 --> 00:54:49,054
And then even to sit down and have coffee,

1022
00:54:49,074 --> 00:54:52,794
the discussion, say, between classes

1023
00:54:52,814 --> 00:54:57,954
usually runs on the basis of babble,

1024
00:54:57,974 --> 00:55:00,114
where we are just talking about things

1025
00:55:00,134 --> 00:55:02,154
that we are not genuinely interested in,

1026
00:55:02,174 --> 00:55:04,714
in order to fill up space.

1027
00:55:04,733 --> 00:55:11,694
This, however, is far more serious a matter

1028
00:55:11,714 --> 00:55:13,954
than simply a description of what's going on.

1029
00:55:13,973 --> 00:55:16,954
So it's a matter of life and death.

1030
00:55:16,973 --> 00:55:17,654
Exactly.

1031
00:55:17,673 --> 00:55:20,694
If the house is burning, I've got to do something.

1032
00:55:20,714 --> 00:55:21,814
Right.

1033
00:55:21,834 --> 00:55:25,394
It isn't, I'm going to discuss who burned the house.

1034
00:55:25,413 --> 00:55:26,134
No.

1035
00:55:26,154 --> 00:55:28,084
What colour his hair was, whether

1036
00:55:28,084 --> 00:55:30,014
it was black or white or purple.

1037
00:55:30,033 --> 00:55:31,654
I want to put that fire out.

1038
00:55:31,673 --> 00:55:34,094
Yes. Or if such and such had not happened,

1039
00:55:34,113 --> 00:55:34,574
the house would not have been burned.

1040
00:55:34,574 --> 00:55:35,413
The house would not be burned.

1041
00:55:35,434 --> 00:55:37,014
I mean, that's all.

1042
00:55:37,033 --> 00:55:39,014
Right. I know. I know.

1043
00:55:39,033 --> 00:55:43,814
And I feel it's so urgent,

1044
00:55:43,834 --> 00:55:45,684
because I see it in India,

1045
00:55:45,684 --> 00:55:47,534
I see it in Europe and America,

1046
00:55:47,554 --> 00:55:51,873
everywhere I go, this sense of slackness,

1047
00:55:51,894 --> 00:55:55,454
sense of despair,

1048
00:55:55,473 --> 00:56:01,514
and sense of hopeless activity that's going on.

1049
00:56:01,534 --> 00:56:04,454
So to come back to what we were saying,

1050
00:56:04,574 --> 00:56:11,074
relationship is the highest importance.

1051
00:56:11,094 --> 00:56:14,394
When in that relationship there is conflict,

1052
00:56:14,414 --> 00:56:21,954
we produce a society which will further that conflict,

1053
00:56:21,974 --> 00:56:25,374
through education, through national sovereignty,

1054
00:56:25,394 --> 00:56:26,984
through all the rest of it

1055
00:56:26,984 --> 00:56:28,574
that's going on in the world.

1056
00:56:28,594 --> 00:56:31,534
So a serious man, serious in

1057
00:56:31,534 --> 00:56:34,474
the sense who is really concerned

1058
00:56:34,494 --> 00:56:34,534
about the world, is a serious man.

1059
00:56:34,534 --> 00:56:34,544
So a serious man, serious in

1060
00:56:34,544 --> 00:56:34,554
the sense who is really concerned

1061
00:56:34,554 --> 00:56:35,054
about the world, is a serious man.

1062
00:56:35,074 --> 00:56:41,734
Committed, must give his total attention

1063
00:56:41,754 --> 00:56:48,314
to this question of relationship, freedom and knowledge.

1064
00:56:48,334 --> 00:56:52,434
If I've heard you correctly,

1065
00:56:52,454 --> 00:56:54,164
and I don't mean by that

1066
00:56:54,164 --> 00:56:55,874
words that have passed between us,

1067
00:56:55,894 --> 00:56:58,714
but if I have truly heard you,

1068
00:56:58,734 --> 00:57:04,474
I've heard something very terrifying,

1069
00:57:04,474 --> 00:57:12,234
that this disorder that in part we have described

1070
00:57:12,253 --> 00:57:17,533
has a built-in necessity in it.

1071
00:57:17,554 --> 00:57:24,533
As long as it persists, it can never change.

1072
00:57:24,554 --> 00:57:26,594
It can never change.

1073
00:57:26,614 --> 00:57:31,794
Any modification of it is more of the same.

1074
00:57:31,814 --> 00:57:34,393
Yes, more of the same. More of the same.

1075
00:57:34,394 --> 00:57:36,864
I have the feeling, and

1076
00:57:36,864 --> 00:57:39,334
I hope I've understood you correctly,

1077
00:57:39,354 --> 00:57:43,534
that there's a relationship between

1078
00:57:43,534 --> 00:57:47,714
the starkness of this necessity

1079
00:57:47,734 --> 00:57:52,174
and the fact that there cannot be a gradual progress,

1080
00:57:52,194 --> 00:57:55,094
or as a philosopher would

1081
00:57:55,094 --> 00:57:57,994
put it, something like essential progress.

1082
00:57:58,014 --> 00:57:59,734
No, no, no.

1083
00:57:59,754 --> 00:58:04,314
But nevertheless there is some demonic progress

1084
00:58:04,314 --> 00:58:08,634
that takes place within this disorder

1085
00:58:08,654 --> 00:58:11,864
that is not so much a progress

1086
00:58:11,864 --> 00:58:15,074
as it is a proliferation of the same.

1087
00:58:15,094 --> 00:58:17,254
And necessarily so. Quite.

1088
00:58:17,274 --> 00:58:18,594
Isn't that what you've been saying?

1089
00:58:18,614 --> 00:58:20,014
Yes. Necessarily so.

1090
00:58:20,034 --> 00:58:22,084
You know that word progress,

1091
00:58:22,084 --> 00:58:24,134
I was told the other day,

1092
00:58:24,154 --> 00:58:29,874
meant entering into enemy's country fully armed.

1093
00:58:29,894 --> 00:58:31,894
Really?

1094
00:58:31,906 --> 00:58:34,646
おぉ…

1095
00:58:34,658 --> 00:58:38,318
Progress is entering into an enemy's country.

1096
00:58:38,338 --> 00:58:41,378
Fully armed. Fully armed.

1097
00:58:41,398 --> 00:58:43,638
Dear me.

1098
00:58:43,658 --> 00:58:45,718
Sir, this is what's happening.

1099
00:58:45,738 --> 00:58:48,518
Oh, I know.

1100
00:58:48,538 --> 00:58:53,158
Next time we converse, the next time,

1101
00:58:53,178 --> 00:58:56,518
I would like very much, if you'd be good enough,

1102
00:58:56,538 --> 00:59:00,598
